# Desktop conveniences (0.0.5g): the right-click menu on the desktop, a
# double-click on a title bar maximising the window, dragging a maximised
# window off the top restoring it, dropping a window at the left edge
# snapping it to half the screen, the Alt+Tab switcher, Super+D (show the
# desktop) twice, Print Screen saving a BMP file, and the shell's history
# (Up) and Tab completion. Coordinates assume the 1280x800 test display and
# the Settings window opening centred (frame 290,92, 700x560).
gui: desktop up at 1280x800
cerberus kernel shell
# Right-click the desktop; the menu's second item is Settings.
!mouseto 600 650
!button right down
!button right up
!wait 0.4
!screenshot build/qol-1.png
!mouseto 640 627
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.6
# Double-click its title bar: maximised (caption buttons move to x=1250).
!mouseto 500 107
!dblclick
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/qol-2.png
# Drag it off the top (it takes its old size again), on to the left edge,
# and drop it: snapped to the left half.
!mouseto 500 20
!button left down
!mouse 0 200
!mouse -600 0
!wait 0.3
!screenshot build/qol-3.png
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/qol-4.png
# Alt+Tab goes to the next window (the terminal); Super+D hides everything,
# Print Screen saves the screen, Super+D brings the windows back.
!keys alt tab
!wait 0.5
!keys meta_l d
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/qol-5.png
!keys print
!wait 1
!keys meta_l d
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/qol-6.png
# The terminal: a command, Up + Enter repeats it; "hel" + Tab completes.
!mouseto 120 400
!button left down
!button left up
!key ticks
!wait 0.5
ticks=
!keys up
!wait 0.3
!keys ret
!wait 0.5
ticks=
!keys h
!keys e
!keys l
!keys tab
!keys ret
!wait 1
help [command|tests]
!key ls /tmp
!wait 1
screenshot-1.bmp
